\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces  Rayleigh BIC in an underwater acoustic metagrating. (a) Periodic two-groove surface and unit-cell dimensions. (b) Complex acoustic band structure; color gives $\qopname  \relax o{log}_{10}Q$, with vivid colors denoting high $Q$. The purple point is a symmetry-protected $\Gamma $ BIC, whereas the red points mark the reciprocal Rayleigh-BIC pair. (c) Local branch: $\mathrm  {Re}\,\Omega _p$ reaches the $n=-1$ Rayleigh line as $Q$ diverges. (d) Homogeneous Floquet pressure amplitudes: $A_0$ and $A_{-1}$ vanish together. (e) Order-resolved exterior eigenfields at the $\Gamma $ BIC, the Rayleigh BIC, and beyond the opening.}}{3}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:eigen}{{2}{3}{Rayleigh BIC in an underwater acoustic metagrating. (a) Periodic two-groove surface and unit-cell dimensions. (b) Complex acoustic band structure; color gives $\log _{10}Q$, with vivid colors denoting high $Q$. The purple point is a symmetry-protected $\Gamma $ BIC, whereas the red points mark the reciprocal Rayleigh-BIC pair. (c) Local branch: $\mathrm {Re}\,\Omega _p$ reaches the $n=-1$ Rayleigh line as $Q$ diverges. (d) Homogeneous Floquet pressure amplitudes: $A_0$ and $A_{-1}$ vanish together. (e) Order-resolved exterior eigenfields at the $\Gamma $ BIC, the Rayleigh BIC, and beyond the opening}{figure.2}{}}
