\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces  Two-coordinate source reduction of the Rayleigh BIC. (a) Periodic cavity lattice with intracell and intercell coupling. (b) Bloch hybridization changes the large- and small-cavity weights and their relative phase. (c,d) At the BIC, the two groove source terms have equal magnitudes and a $\pi $ phase difference in both the $n=0$ and $n=-1$ radiation rows. The strict pressure zeros are obtained from the full eigenproblem in Fig.\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:eigen}.}}{4}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:mechanism}{{3}{4}{Two-coordinate source reduction of the Rayleigh BIC. (a) Periodic cavity lattice with intracell and intercell coupling. (b) Bloch hybridization changes the large- and small-cavity weights and their relative phase. (c,d) At the BIC, the two groove source terms have equal magnitudes and a $\pi $ phase difference in both the $n=0$ and $n=-1$ radiation rows. The strict pressure zeros are obtained from the full eigenproblem in Fig.~\ref {fig:eigen}}{figure.3}{}}
